  "notes": "This portable C++ scenario uses only the official IEEE 1516.1 RTIambassador API and standard library. It passes the standard SUPPORT_SERVICES group plus valid federate, object-class, interaction-class, and live object-instance handles from a joined peer to a disconnected ambassador, a connected ambassador that has not joined, and the same ambassador after it joins and resigns while remaining connected. It asserts only the declared NotConnected and FederateNotExecutionMember boundaries, not normalization values or provider-specific handle representation.",
